  "title": "Full adder",
  "format": "build",
  "skills": [
    "logic.full-adder",
    "logic.carry"
  ],
  "brief": {
    "story": "The half adder couldn’t take a carry from the column before. A full adder adds three bits (A, B and carry in): SUM = A ⊕ B ⊕ Cin and COUT = A·B + Cin·(A ⊕ B). Two XORs, two ANDs and an OR, on three chips. The OR that makes the carry isn’t fed.",
    "goal": "Wire the two AND outputs (columns 13 and 16) into the OR gate (columns 21 and 22) so SUM and COUT add A + B + Cin.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "Full adder",
      "rows": [
        [
          "IC1 74HC86",
          "P = A ⊕ B · SUM = P ⊕ Cin"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 74HC08",
          "A·B → column 13 · Cin·P → column 16"
        ],
        [
          "IC3 74HC32",
          "pins 1, 2 = columns 21, 22 → COUT"
        ],
        [
          "1 + 1 + 1",
          "= 11: SUM 1, COUT 1"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "The carry out is 1 when A and B are both 1, or when the carry in meets a single 1 (P = A ⊕ B). IC2 makes both of those; IC3 ORs them.",
    "A·B comes out on column 13, Cin·P on column 16. IC3’s inputs are pins 1 and 2: columns 21 and 22.",
    "Column 13 → column 21, and column 16 → column 22."
  ],
