  "debrief": "A full adder adds three bits: the two digits and the carry from the column to the right. Chain eight of them, each COUT into the next one’s Cin, and you have an 8-bit adder: the ripple-carry adder at the heart of every early CPU. Your phone adds the same way, just faster and wider."
